{
  "summary": "Enforces that invalid ValidationState instances specify both a valid failure Result enum and a non-empty reject reason via runtime Assumes. Adds a new BlockValidationResult::BLOCK_INCONCLUSIVE enum value across validation, net processing, and the kernel C API, using it in TestBlockValidity when a block does not connect to the active chain tip.",
  "problem": "ValidationState allowed callers to mark a validation state invalid without setting a specific result enum or providing a reject reason. PR #31981 introduced an instance in TestBlockValidity where an invalid state was returned with an unset result when checking a block against a non-best chain tip, leaving callers and APIs with ambiguous error state.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'PR #31981 moved a previous-block check from outside of TestBlockValidity() to inside it, and introduced a new usage of BlockValidationState with unset result.'",
    "Commit e6f4f48c15: 'Ensure that an Invalid ValidationState, constructed through Invalid(), always has a set result field, by using an Assume. This increases code robustness/security.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
   "depends_on": [],
   "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Extends the kernel C API and wrapper with btck_BlockValidationResult_INCONCLUSIVE.",
  "changed_since_previous": "No functional changes; the PR was rebased.",
  "card": "This PR enforces that all invalid ValidationState objects contain an explicit error result enum and a non-empty reject reason, backed by runtime Assumes. It introduces BlockValidationResult::BLOCK_INCONCLUSIVE across validation, net processing, and the kernel C API, resolving an instance in TestBlockValidity where an invalid state was returned with an unset result. In P2P processing, inconclusive results explicitly bypass peer punishment.",
